{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016356-what-kind-of-spheres-would-freddy-krueger-use","id":1016356,"title":"What kind of spheres would Freddy Krueger use?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-12T19:08:21-08:00","id":1016356,"title":"What kind of spheres would Freddy Krueger use?","content":"This may sound silly, but hear me out.<br /> <br /> For those of you who are unaware, Freddy Krueger is a horror character who manifests in the dreams of his victims and kills them. In the dream world, he has near unlimited power to do as he pleases to his victims, in the real world, he's powerless.<br /> <br /> So, necessarily, what kind of spheres would he have, if he were bound by World of Darkness mechanics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T19:13:14-08:00","id":1016358,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I'd sooner write up Freddy Krueger as a spirit or even a ghost before trying to fit him into the Mage mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T19:18:24-08:00","id":1016360,"title":"","content":"Spirits can have Sphere based charms if need be.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Mind 5 to do all the dream stuff, possibly higher if you wanted to go into Archmage territory. Arguably Life 3 or Entropy 4 in order to physically kill through mental attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T19:23:29-08:00","id":1016361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016356-what-kind-of-spheres-would-freddy-krueger-use?p=1016360#post1016360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits can have Sphere based charms if need be.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Mind 5 to do all the dream stuff, possibly higher if you wanted to go into Archmage territory. Arguably Life 3 or Entropy 4 in order to physically kill through mental attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, if it's a vampire I imagine I'd need matter, yes?<br /> <br /> And even so, how would I be able to kill creatively without spheres like telekensis (to throw them around in their mind) and so on? All life could do is effect their patterns","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T19:59:01-08:00","id":1016372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016356-what-kind-of-spheres-would-freddy-krueger-use?p=1016361#post1016361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now, if it's a vampire I imagine I'd need matter, yes?<br /> <br /> And even so, how would I be able to kill creatively without spheres like telekensis (to throw them around in their mind) and so on? All life could do is effect their patterns</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depends how you view it. Mind 5 lets you basically implant memories wholesale. You can make them think they're being flung around the room and use Life to make them feel it too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T09:31:38-08:00","id":1016602,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd say if you're going the Sphere route Life 3 is a necessity to make dream wounds reflect on the dreamers' bodies in the waking world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T10:06:37-08:00","id":1018132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016356-what-kind-of-spheres-would-freddy-krueger-use?p=1016361#post1016361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now, if it's a vampire I imagine I'd need matter, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>(Just jumping in...)<br /> No, not necessarily. People sometimes confuse/conflate the innate qualities of vampires wherein to use a Life Effect on them you normally need to use a degree of Matter conjunctionally due to their metaphysical natures, with *always* having to have that when some other Spheres are applied and/or when Life might act in a support manner with another Sphere (Entropy, in this case) in a manner that that isn't transforming/harming-healing the vampire in a direct way. The Mind aspects (which levels 3/4 are actually sufficient to do most of what Freddy does; Mind:5 would be needed for him to continue existing indefinitely as an &quot;astral shade&quot;, as it were, but otherwise he can do most of what he does -- influence dreams, cause psycho-physiological harm, and similar -- with Mind:4) don't require conjunctional Life for most purposes relative to vampires. Similarly, using Entropy:4 doesn't require Matter, either, in this context. (The Life aspects linked to Entropy in some of the (E)ffects implied wouldn't require Matter for a vampire, but some would -- it depends on the very specific instances/aspects being applied.) Example: using Entropy:4 to harm the vampire via casual causality influences doesn't require Matter b/c Life isn't included; tangentially, however, the *directive* aspects of Entropy:4 can be targeted/supported by Life:1/2 when directing &quot;x&quot; against a vampire, and in that context Matter, again, *isn't* required conjunctionally. (If, however, one was using Entropy:4 to &quot;infect&quot; the vampire with blood-born diseases/poisons that he might be vulnerable to and Life was used to *enhance* said factors, *then* Matter would have to be used also due to the vampires paranormal physiology. Some fine lines get covered and crossed depending on the specifics involved with each example...)<br /> <br /> But then, Mage(tm) has always been about subtle distinctions... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}